{
 "text": "Governments all over Europe just shut down their own websites on purpose because of this bug where anyone could take over a site without a password. It's in PHP, the language everyone loves and about 7 out of 10 websites run on it. It was in there for like 14 years before some researchers using AI figured out how bad it was. They gave the PHP people a heads up so they could fix it first, but word got out a day early and hackers were already trying it. Cloudflare says, once it was official, they saw tens of thousands of attempts in 45 minutes, and then millions. And the fix doesn't help until somebody actually installs it on every single server. Plus, about half of PHP sites are on versions so old, they're not officially supported anymore. So even the FBI said, if you can't update yet, just turn it off. Which is basically what tech support tells you about everything. And that's pretty much what those governments already did.",
